# 16. Gunicorn Deployment Issues

## Problem

The Flask application worked with:

```bash
python3 app.py
```

but failed under production deployment.

## Cause

Flask’s built-in development server is not suitable for production environments.

## Solution

Installed and configured Gunicorn:

```bash
pip install gunicorn
```

Started Gunicorn manually:

```bash
gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:5000 app:app
```

Created a systemd service for persistence and automatic startup.

## What I Learned

* Difference between development and production servers
* WSGI server architecture
* Importance of Gunicorn in production deployments

---

# 17. Systemd Service Configuration

## Problem

The Gunicorn process stopped after reboot or terminal logout.

## Cause

The application was not configured as a system service.

## Solution

Created a systemd service file:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/nasa.service
```

Enabled the service:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl start nasa
sudo systemctl enable nasa
```

Verified service status:

```bash
sudo systemctl status nasa
```

## What I Learned

* Linux service management
* Boot-time application startup
* Process persistence in production systems

